toolUseResult.stdout:
The cache-split commit (7f3e9c68) moved profile/MEMORY.md out of the
SessionStart dispatcher and into Pi's `systemPrompt:build` profile-base
filter so the stable global profile rides Pi's cross-cwd cacheable base.
But that filter only runs inside Pi. Claude Code and Codex reach memory
solely through `harness-cli.dispatchSessionStart`, so dropping profile
there silently starved them of global preferences — only project memory
surfaced. (cross-harness-smoke.spec.ts asserts both must surface; the
cache-split commit updated the unit specs but overlooked the e2e one.)

Fix is client-aware: the dispatcher emits profile + project for non-Pi
clients (their only channel) and stays project-only for Pi (whose
before_agent_start owns profile via the base filter / tail fallback, so
emitting it here would double-inject and burst the prompt cache).

Also reset the process-lifetime profile snapshot on session_start: a
background dream run may rewrite profile/MEMORY.md between sessions, and
a new session must pick up changed memory by content. The memo stays
stable within a session (byte-stable base) and across sub-agents (they
don't fire session_start). This was a second latent failure in the same
cross-harness test, masked because it died on the first assertion.

Tests: split the dispatcher unit test into a Pi (project-only) case and
a Claude/Codex (profile+project) case; full suite green + typecheck.

